@startuml global-key

title GlobalKey – Cross-Widget State Access

skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor<<key>> LightYellow
}

participant "MainShell" as MS
participant "_recordKey\nGlobalKey<RecordPageState>" as GK <<key>>
participant "RecordPage" as RP
participant "Settings" as ST

MS -> GK : create
MS -> RP : key: _recordKey\nonGoToEasyTwo / onGoToSettings
MS -> ST : recordKey: _recordKey

note over GK
  GlobalKey gives direct access
  to a specific widget's State
  anywhere in the tree
end note

== User types new WCA-ID in Settings ==

ST -> GK : recordKey.currentState?.setState((){})
GK -> RP : triggers rebuild of RecordPageState
RP -> RP : _getWcaData()\n(fetches new WCA-ID from AppSettings)

== User opens Record screen from closed ==

MS -> RP : new RecordPage(key: _recordKey, ...)
note right : key ensures Flutter reuses\nthe same State instance

@enduml
